# Derived by hand from the dynamic law (Semantics R2/R3) as ruled for structural dynamics: with S(n) the snapshot as the last act of n's construction, the dynamic after m is S(m-1) (after the build, S(0)); it fires at n+1 with S(n) when S(n) differs from S(n-1), owing that tick; samples at n+1 read S(n-1), from n+2 S(n); the host's supplier rows read the child's structure directly, so a newborn place is forwarded in its tick (R7, ch. 9).
